  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Hi Dev. I haven't added you to eng-deploy-tools yet, because it needs one more approval.\n\n- **Your manager's approval is on file.** Sofia Andersson approved it on October 26 (APR-3102).\n- **The group needs Security approval too.** eng-deploy-tools is nested inside release-operators, which sits inside prod-admins (privileged). That makes the group privileged for approval purposes, so Security must sign off as well. I've sent that request to Jun Ortiz on the Security approvers list (APR-4001), and it's pending.\n\nOnce Jun approves, I can add you to the group. If you'd like it sooner, you can ask Jun directly. Your ticket T-6003 is set to pending approval."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ugh, I didn't know it was nested like that. I thought it was just the standard deploy group. Why does it need Security if Sofia already signed off? Fine, I'll ping Jun. Is there anything I can do on my end to speed it up?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Security approval is required because of how the groups are nested. Your access to eng-deploy-tools also carries the access level of the groups it sits inside. Sofia's approval covers the manager requirement, but a privileged group also needs a Security sign-off. Sofia can't give that.\n\nTo speed it up:\n\n- **Ping Jun Ortiz** and ask him to review APR-4001 in the approval system. A short note on why you need the deploy tools will help him decide quickly.\n- **Make sure the request is in the approval system.** Approvals only count when they're recorded there, so a chat message to Jun won't be enough on its own.\n\nI can't make the approval faster from my side. Once Jun approves, tell me, or I'll check the status when you come back, and then add you to the group."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so I'll message Jun with a quick note on why I need the deploy tools. Quick check: is APR-4001 the request I should point him to, or is there a separate one for me? And do you know roughly how long Security approvals usually take?"
